    "naming_convention_prompt": "## Lab Naming Convention\n\nThis laboratory uses non-standard population names. You MUST use these exact names in your hierarchy:\n\n- **Krondule Cells**: defined by `Exclude variable flow rate`\n- **Quixar Subset**: defined by `SSC-A vs SSC-H`\n- **Threxix Population**: defined by `FSC-A vs FSC-H`\n- **Splonix Subset**: defined by `FSC vs SSC (debris exclusion)`\n- **Glorp Cells**: defined by `NOT SLAN+++ CD64+++ AND NOT CD11b- CD36+++`\n- **Nimbular Cells**: defined by `CD45+`\n- **Frimblax Population**: defined by `CD66b-`\n- **Morglian Cells**: defined by `Lin- TLR2+ (Lin = CD3, CD19, CD56, CD123)`\n- **Plixnor Cells**: defined by `CD14++ CD16-`\n- **Zymbrix Subset**: defined by `CX3CR1lo CCR2hi`\n- **Zanthrex Population**: defined by `CD16mid-hi CD14var`\n- **Grindlax Cells**: defined by `CX3CR1+ CCR2lo-int`\n- **Qwelnar Cells**: defined by `CCR2+ SLAN-`\n- **Wumbus Cells**: defined by `CCR2- SLAN-`\n- **Snorfalax Population**: defined by `CCR2- SLAN+`\n\nUse standard names (Singlets, Lymphocytes, Live) for QC gates only.\n",
